From 8c53116991513f4e9b907f39bfbf7e4e6a586ec5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:03:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 09/14] yblod-engine-vk: specialized pipelines; pack chroma
 filtered per block

Register pressure, measured with Mesa's V3D drm-shim (V3D 7.1, Mesa
26.2.2): every pack variant and fel_chroma compiled to 2 threads per QPU,
fel_chroma and many pack variants spilling. V3D hides memory latency with
threads (4 need <= 32 registers each).

- Specialization: a frame's uniform selectors (EL filter, chroma method,
  dual MMR, MMR kinds, top-left siting, CB1's Annex B chroma) become
  specialization constants 20.. (SPEC_OR_PUSH: 255 = the push constant, the
  generic pipelines unchanged). The engine makes each variant on first use
  (pack, fel_chroma, luma_phase_guide, mmr_dual_horizontal), keyed by every
  constant; DVVK_SPECIALIZE=0 keeps the generic ones, DVVK_PREPARE_VARIANTS=1
  makes the usual variants at startup. fel_chroma: 6612 instructions,
  23:13 spills -> 373..2628, no spills, polynomial-chroma variants at 4
  threads.
- pack: the sited 4:2:0 chroma is filtered per block right after its rows
  are fetched (sited_chroma), kept as cb | cr << 16, and the prefetched luma
  as its two loaded words: 32 row values no longer live through the pixel
  loop. Peak registers ~60 -> 32..37 in the specialized variants; the
  compiler now unrolls its loops (12-13 -> 1). Still 2 threads.

Outputs unchanged: Annex B and nearest byte-identical to before, specialized
and generic; bilinear's specialized fused path equal to the generic staged
reference (DVVK_VERIFY); P010 == SAND == Pi mode; CB1 == Vulkan; clean under
the validation layer.
